Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 04:30:00 +0000
Subject: csm-manager.c: Connect a client's "disconnected" signal only once

on_store_client_added() connects "disconnected" for every client added to
the client store, and on_xsmp_client_register_request() connected it a
second time when an XSMP client registered. on_client_disconnected() then
ran twice for every registered XSMP client: the client was disconnected,
its inhibitors removed and its app's restart logic run twice, and the
store removal was repeated.

XSMP clients are added to the store when their connection is accepted,
before they can register, so the store's connection is enough.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5
---
--- a/cinnamon-session/csm-manager.c
+++ b/cinnamon-session/csm-manager.c
@@ -2984,11 +2984,6 @@ on_xsmp_client_register_request (CsmXSMP
 
         g_debug ("CsmManager: Adding new client %s to session", new_id);
 
-        g_signal_connect (client,
-                          "disconnected",
-                          G_CALLBACK (on_client_disconnected),
-                          manager);
-
         /* If it's a brand new client id, we just accept the client*/
         if (IS_STRING_EMPTY (*id)) {
                 goto out;
